error[RB0323]: cannot tell what `T` of `Pair` is: the fields give `int` and `string`
  --> RB0323-uninferred-type-argument.road:10:42
   |
10 |     on Ping -> Idle  set text = describe(Pair { first: 1, second: "one" })
   |                                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: use the value where a `Pair<…>` is expected, such as a `set` of a variable of that type, so that its type arguments are known

error[RB0323]: `T` of `Pair` would be `event Ping`, and an event cannot be a type argument
  --> RB0323-uninferred-type-argument.road:14:42
   |
14 |     on Ping -> Idle  set text = describe(Pair { first: event, second: event })
   |                                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: give the value a declared type: `set` it to a variable of type `Pair<…>`, or pass it where one is expected
